        "owner": "hp",
        "atoms": [
          "Oct to Nov 2025",
          "I enabled HP teams to expand Copilot use into reusable workflows and skills for recurring tasks, with hands-on labs in requirements translation, rapid prototyping, and IT troubleshooting."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "hp-foundations",
        "owner": "hp",
        "atoms": [
          "AI Foundations for Digital Innovators",
          "Oct 2025",
          "How large language models work and where they fail, from bias to hallucination; choosing among ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Copilot, Perplexity, and NotebookLM; the H4W and COSTAR prompt frameworks; and AI across the software development lifecycle.",
          "Participants rewrote one message for four audiences, built a slide deck from three reports, and generated a clickable prototype in Gemini."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "hp-solutions",
        "owner": "hp",
        "atoms": [
          "Applying AI in IT and Digital Solutions",
          "Nov 12, 2025",
          "Retrieval-augmented generation, vector databases, and knowledge graphs; custom GPTs; the difference between AI workflows and agents, and a checklist for when an agent is worth building; and AI governance. Participants built a business-requirements translator and designed an IT troubleshooting agent."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "hp-title",
        "owner": "hp",
        "atoms": [
          "Applied AI for IT teams"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "morgan-brief",
        "owner": "morgan-lewis",
        "atoms": [
          "AI adoption and change-management workshop · Morgan Lewis",
          "I trained the firm’s internal trainers and champions to help initially resistant lawyers adopt AI, turning real objections into live roleplay and reusable enablement toolkits."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "morgan-adoption",
        "owner": "morgan-lewis",
        "atoms": [
          "Why adoption fails",
          "The innovation adoption curve, Deloitte Business Chemistry, and the MAPPR model for diagnosing resistance: Motivation, Ability, Permission, Proof, and Reinforcement."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "morgan-roleplay",
        "owner": "morgan-lewis",
        "atoms": [
          "From resistance to persuasion",
          "Participants listed why partners, associates, and staff would refuse AI.",
          "Gemini sorted that board into ten resister personas, from the accuracy skeptic to the billable-hour traditionalist.",
          "In a live roleplay, Gemini played one persona while I used the CLEAR framework to win them over."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "morgan-toolkit",
        "owner": "morgan-lewis",
        "atoms": [
          "Groups then wrote persuasion messages for their own persona and designed a champion’s toolkit: a green, yellow, and red guide to which tasks are safe for AI, office hours, flash cards, and prompt-off competitions."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "morgan-title",
        "owner": "morgan-lewis",
        "atoms": [
          "Training the AI champions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pbs-brief",
        "owner": "pbs",
        "atoms": [
          "AI strategy session · PBS"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pbs-foundations",
        "owner": "pbs",
        "atoms": [
          "AI foundations",
          "What generative AI is and isn’t, how large language models work, and where they fail."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pbs-governance",
        "owner": "pbs",
        "atoms": [
          "Data privacy and governance first",
          "Privacy and governance frameworks as the first step, and how they set what AI can safely be used for."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pbs-workflow",
        "owner": "pbs",
        "atoms": [
          "Start with the pain points that take employees’ time away from work central to the mission.",
          "Break each pain point into a list of steps.",
          "Run those steps with a deterministic script, workflow, or skill."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pbs-coordination",
        "owner": "pbs",
        "atoms": [
          "When the automations need coordinating, add simple agents, and let the coordination grow more complex rather than the agents themselves.",
          "Keep each agent simple enough to audit, and put the complexity in the relationships between agents."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pbs-title",
        "owner": "pbs",
        "atoms": [
          "AI strategy, governance first"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sonova-progression",
        "owner": "sonova",
        "atoms": [
          "I built a beginner-to-advanced progression from prompting to reusable workflows, inventory tracking, and prediction use cases.",
          "Participants tested budget-analysis software against live formulas, edge cases, and invented explanations, then turned corrections into reusable rules."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sonova-title",
        "owner": "sonova",
        "atoms": [
          "From prompting to reliable workflows"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "cmu-accepted",
        "owner": "cmu-teaching",
        "atoms": [
          "Web Applications Course Developer · Teaching Assistant",
          "May 2013 to Dec 2013",
          "Instructed 105+ students as Agile Product Owner for their final projects."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "cmu-curriculum",
        "owner": "cmu-teaching",
        "atoms": [
          "Redesigned the Web Applications course with the professor, planning a 20-lecture semester from client-side code and HTTP through relational and NoSQL databases, servlets, security, and Django, plus a follow-on Web Application Frameworks course."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "cmu-exercises",
        "owner": "cmu-teaching",
        "atoms": [
          "Teaching",
          "Created a cloud platform for course administration.",
          "Built the client-side exercise set: HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript demos, from form validation and a calculator to single-player Pong and an image gallery, each with extension exercises.",
          "Designed server-side exercises on sessions, cookies, and relational databases, an HTML-injection exercise on Django template escaping, and a deliberately flawed Django app for students to expose by writing tests."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "cmu-frameworks",
        "owner": "cmu-teaching",
        "atoms": [
          "Built reference survey apps in Spring MVC, Play, and Django, taking the Spring version through six releases on Google App Engine with image upload, AJAX editing, and survey recommendations."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "atos-accepted",
        "owner": "atos",
        "atoms": [
          "Presented how graphs enrich questions and check generated answers, how to choose model size, and how to set up a local model live."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "atos-talk",
        "owner": "atos",
        "atoms": [
          "Knowledge Graphs, Then Small Language Models",
          "Presented what a knowledge graph is, how it enriches questions before they reach a model, and how it checks the model’s answer afterward,",
          "then where graphs go next: sub-graphs by topic, failure graphs, codified expertise, and the graph behind an API.",
          "Covered small language models next: what they are, when to go small and when to go big, a live setup of a local model in five minutes, and how they change the way people work."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "atos-deck",
        "owner": "atos",
        "atoms": [
          "Open the deck"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "topic-1",
        "owner": "talks",
        "atoms": [
          "From architecture to adoption",
          "Why technical decisions only matter when teams can carry them into the organization."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "topic-2",
        "owner": "talks",
        "atoms": [
          "Engineering leadership in the agentic era",
          "How management systems change when software production becomes abundant."
        ]
